        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Leafs' offseason hums with quiet ambition even after finishing 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, a final record that forced a hard reset rather than a hopeful roll. <strong>Gavin McKenna, the club's No. 1 draft pick, signed his entry-level contract July 3 and is already expected to play for Toronto</strong>, signaling a commitment to youth alongside the veteran flair they added earlier in free agency, including star goalie Sergei Bobrovsky. While chatter swirls about Patrick Kane and Elias Pettersson, GM Brad Treliving has taken a measured approach, letting preliminary talks cool before committing to big cap hits. Former assistant GM Brandon Pridham's departure to Pittsburgh underscores the front office's churn, yet Adam Copeland insists John Chayka has already silenced skeptics with these early moves. <strong>What to watch: whether McKenna cracks the 2026-27 roster out of camp, and if Treliving adds one more impact forward before the season opens</strong>.",
